# Guard film (climbing done once for every body, 2026-10-18, docs/plans/climbing-every-body.md): the king termite up a
# pillar two blocks high, over its top and head first down the far side onto the floor, then away from it, with its
# own body's numbers (its feet, its soft abdomen in segments following the path, its lift and push on the wall). The
# abdomen must follow each edge, never into the stone or out into the air; the body tips over an edge from when its
# front feet reach it until its hind feet are over. The king walks slowly, so it starts near the pillar and gets more
# time (with 80 ticks from 0.5 it had not reached the top when told to go on, and backed off the wall).
cmd time set noon
cmd weather clear
cmd fill 3 -60 0 3 -59 0 stone
lens 30
walker termite_king 2.0 -60 0.5 -90
log king
cmd tick freeze
fov 10
follow 0 0.15 -7 0 0
go 3 -58 0
burst up 130 1
go 5 -60 0
burst down 130 1
log off
follow off
quit
